    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d464">

                <pb facs="0553" n="473" xml:id="pg473"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr.
                            Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-05-22"><hi rendition="#italic">May 22,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 636.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s No. 482,
                    of November I last, you are instructed to report what action you have taken in
                    the matter of the request that Mr. William F. Smith, an American citizen,
                    detained on St. Helena as a prisoner of war, be released on parole.</p>
                <p>In consequence of a letter from the Hon. Frank E. Wilson, M. C., of the 16th
                    instant, you are instructed to recall the matter to the attention of the British
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
